# project: dc-exit-to-cloud
VAR wave = 0
VAR rollbacks = 0

-> wave_planning

=== wave_planning ===
Sequence the 30 applications into three migration waves, easiest first.
Done when the wave assignments are agreed and the steering committee approves the sequencing.
* [Steering committee approves wave sequencing] @human -> wave_kickoff

=== wave_kickoff ===
The current wave formally starts: teams, change windows and rollback criteria for this wave are locked in.
~ wave += 1
~ rollbacks = 0
+ [Wave underway] -> replatform_wave

=== replatform_wave ===
Replatform every application in the current wave onto the cloud target.
Done when each app is deployed to the cloud environment and passing its build and smoke checks.
+ [Wave replatformed] -> parallel_run

=== parallel_run ===
Run the replatformed wave in parallel against production for two weeks, comparing outputs and data.
+ [Two weeks clean, no data divergence] -> cutover
+ [Parallel run shows data divergence] -> rollback_wave

=== rollback_wave ===
Roll the whole wave back to the data center and diagnose the divergence.
~ rollbacks += 1
+ {rollbacks < 2} [Fix and retry the wave] ~loop~ -> replatform_wave
+ {rollbacks >= 2} [Second rollback on this wave — escalate] -> steering_review

=== steering_review ===
The steering committee reviews the wave's approach before a third try is permitted.
+ [Revised approach approved, retry the wave] @human ~loop~ -> replatform_wave
* [Approach not viable, halt the programme] @human -> END

=== cutover ===
Cut the wave over app by app during agreed change windows until every app in the wave serves from the cloud.
+ [All apps in the wave cut over] -> wave_stability

=== wave_stability ===
The wave runs in production from the cloud; monitor until it is judged stable.
+ {wave < 3} [Wave stable, seek go-ahead for the next wave] -> next_wave_gate
+ {wave >= 3} [Final wave stable] -> final_stability_watch

=== next_wave_gate ===
The steering committee gates the start of the next wave on the previous wave's stability.
+ [Committee approves the next wave] @human ~loop~ -> wave_kickoff
+ [Hold — stability concerns to resolve first] @human ~loop~ -> wave_stability

=== final_stability_watch ===
The last wave runs stably; the clock runs on 30 consecutive days of stability.
* [30 days of stability reached] -> exit_negotiation

=== exit_negotiation ===
Negotiate the data center contract exit: notice, terms and exit timeline.
* [Exit terms agreed] @human -> decommission

=== decommission ===
Physically decommission the data center: wipe, remove and dispose of hardware, and vacate the space.
* [Decommission complete] -> final_termination

=== final_termination ===
Facilities and finance jointly review and sign the final contract termination.
* [Facilities and finance sign the termination] @human -> END
